# deps
**/node_modules

# Local secrets. Broad on purpose: `.env` and `**/.env` alone left `.env.backup`,
# `.env.local` and `.env.old-key.bak` perfectly committable, checked, and they were.
# This repo's predecessor had an admin key in its history from the first commit, which is
# the entire reason it exists as a fresh tree, so the rule is a name prefix and not a
# name.
.env*
**/.env*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# build output
**/dist
app/.vite
server/web

# Images are ignored by default and allowed back by location, so a screenshot dropped
# while debugging cannot drift into the repo. (The old tree accumulated 31 loose PNGs at
# its root, some showing real project names.) Anything that IS an asset lives somewhere
# named, and is listed here.
*.png
!app/public/**/*.png
!docs/images/**/*.png
!.github/assets/**/*.png

# tooling / scratch
.playwright-mcp/
*.log
.codegraph/

# maintainer's own notes: roadmap, shipping plan, night logs. Never public.
private/
CLAUDE.md
